WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:04.119
A privileged container, 3
replicas, shipping to production.

2
00:00:05.950 --> 00:00:06.750
So scan it.

3
00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:08.211
Here is what kube-noob says.

4
00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:11.279
0 findings.

5
00:00:11.279 --> 00:00:14.973
Critical, high, medium,
low: every count is zero.

6
00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:19.631
But the gate does not pass.

7
00:00:19.631 --> 00:00:22.494
It names the object
nothing read, and exits 1.

8
00:00:26.450 --> 00:00:28.508
The container is still privileged.

9
00:00:28.508 --> 00:00:31.838
The kind holding it is one
kube-noob has no reader for,

10
00:00:31.838 --> 00:00:33.533
so its pods were never read.

11
00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:36.910
That is the whole rule.

12
00:00:36.910 --> 00:00:41.924
An absence, an unknown, or a shape it
does not recognise never reads as a pass,

13
00:00:41.924 --> 00:00:43.194
a zero, or complete.

14
00:00:44.383 --> 00:00:46.677
Find out what your own gate did not read.

15
00:00:46.677 --> 00:00:48.244
Get it at kube-noob dot com.
